# The audit log is hash-chained. CRLF injection changes the bytes and breaks
# chain verification on a machine with a different core.autocrlf setting.
*.jsonl -text
*.py text eol=lf

# An OpenTimestamps proof binds exact bytes. CRLF conversion changes them, so a
# stamp made on Windows would fail ots verify on any other machine (edge case e9).
eval_report.md -text
*.ots binary
